   "newText": "When a future grid resembles this pattern, identify the marker/background colors and fill only single-cell horizontal gaps between same-row markers with 2. Verify no unrelated cells or vertical gaps are changed.\n\n### Additional confirmed recurrence evidence: `task-d380c220` (2026-10-21)\n- Demo was 13×21, background 8, marker 0. The output changed every background cell lying between consecutive markers in the same row at a one-cell gap to color 2; e.g. row 3 had markers across alternating columns and the gaps became 2. Markers and all unrelated background cells were preserved. A shorter run with two markers was also bridged; a row with gaps of different lengths showed only single-cell gaps bridged.\n- Test was 27×15, background 9, marker 8. Applied the identical rule: for each row independently, change a 9 to 2 exactly when its immediate left and right neighbors are both 8. Keep all 8s and other 9s. The resulting grid was accepted correct with zero wrong submissions.\n- Thus the rule generalizes across marker/background colors and grid dimensions; it is local horizontal interpolation only, not a global pattern completion and not vertical filling. A simple check is: output[r][c]=2 iff input[r][c] is background and input[r][c-1]=input[r][c+1]=marker; otherwise preserve the input cell."
